# Reviewed credential-scan baseline.
#
# Each line is a fingerprint (path + truncated salted hash), never a value.
# Adding a line means a human decided the finding is not a live credential in
# tracked source. Every entry needs a comment saying why, and a way out.
#
# Format: <path>:<hash>
#
# This file is deliberately empty. An empty baseline is the healthy state: it
# means no tracked file carries a credential, so the scanner needs no
# exceptions to pass. Prefer removing the value over adding a line here.
#
# It could only be emptied once `main` caught up with `dev` (#36). The portal
# headers this branch removes are still present in history, in b5c2edc and
# e69daf2, and the scanner reads ranges rather than tips -- so while those
# commits sat between the two branches, a `dev` -> `main` scan reached them
# and needed the three entries that used to be listed here. They are now
# behind `main`, no future range spans them, and #12 records the exposure.
